<!-- STRUCTURE GUIDE -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Structure Guide</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p class="section-intro">Implement these two classes in <code>student/data_structs.py</code>.</p>
    
    <!-- Stack Guide -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Stack Implementation</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                Use a Python <code>list</code>. The <strong>end</strong> of the list is the "top" of the stack.
                <ul>
                    <li>push: <code>append(item)</code></li>
                    <li>pop: <code>pop()</code> (removes from end)</li>
                    <li>peek: <code>return list[-1]</code></li>
                    <li>Check for empty before popping/peeking! Return <code>None</code> if empty.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Queue Guide -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Queue Implementation</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                Use <code>collections.deque</code> for efficiency.
                <ul>
                    <li>Import: <code>from collections import deque</code></li>
                    <li>Init: <code>self._items = deque()</code></li>
                    <li>enqueue: <code>append(item)</code></li>
                    <li>dequeue: <code>popleft()</code> (removes from front)</li>
                    <li>front: <code>return deque[0]</code></li>
                    <li>Check for empty! Return <code>None</code> if empty.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

